---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_494",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 494,
  "text": "[[2162.1]] <b>388₆.  De controversiis DE CONTROVERSIIS </p>\n<p> [[2162.4]] Controversiae quemadmodum civiles, ita et sacrae vel ad judicium vel ad causam\n[[2162.5]] pertinent, sive ut vulgo loquuntur vel ad Processum judiciarium, vel ad Merita causae. </p>\n<p> [[2162.6]] Controversiae quae ad Judicium ipsum pertinent, nonnunquam generales, praejudiciales,\n[[2162.7]] liminares dicuntur. Est autem <b>judicium status hominum rationibus\n[[2162.8]] certantium sub exitus sive conclusionis spe.</i> Spes autem victoriae a certo\n[[2162.9]] quodam signo visibili ac nullis disputationibus subjecto pendere debet. Quale est sententia\n[[2162.10]] judicis, persuasio ipsius adversarii, evidentia rationis. </p>\n<p> [[2162.11]] Caetera enim signa pleraque novarum saepe difficultatum feracia sunt. Judex si quid\n[[2162.12]] in sententia sua sit ambiguitatis aut obscuritatis, tollere poterit explicando. Fateor tamen\n[[2162.13]] nullo judice opus fore, si duo litigantes in certam quandam disputandi formam consentirent,\n[[2162.14]] eamque accurate observarent, ita enim sponte naturae veritas vel certe probabilitas\n[[2162.15]] alterutrius opinionis se detegeret, <b>et pro judice esset ratio ipsa.</b> </p>\n<p> [[2162.16]] Opponitur judicium <b>Bello</b>, quod est <i>status</i> hominum <i>per vim certantium</i>, ubi nihil\n[[2162.17]] attinet adjicere exitus spem, cum in ipsa hujus certaminis natura contineatur, provalente\n[[2162.18]] utique potentiore aut feliciore: at vero non omnis status per rationes certantium judicium\n[[2162.19]] est, saepe enim abest spes exitus utroque sententiam ad extremum tuente, auditoribusque\n[[2162.20]] suspensis. </p>\n<p> [[2162.21]] Qui rationibus certant vicisse videbuntur, ubi scopum assecuti erunt, scopus autem\n[[2162.22]] est persuadere. Nam qui sorte, qui monomachia, qui purgatione quam vocant, sive\n[[2162.23]] probatione per ignem aut aquam, denique qui tormentis vincit, is non ideo innocentiam\n[[2163.1]] suam aut adversarii culpam persuadet, aufert tamen praemium, impunitatem scilicet aut\n[[2163.2]] rem de qua agitur. </p>\n",
  "number": "388₆.",
  "title": "De controversiis",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:388₆. De controversiis DE CONTROVERSIIS Controversiae quemadmodum civiles, ita et sacrae vel ad judicium vel ad causam pertinent, sive ut vulgo loquuntur vel ad Processum judiciarium, vel ad Merita causae. Controversiae quae ad Judicium ipsum pertinent, nonnunquam generales, praejudiciales, liminare...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Hidden data for JavaScript -->
      <script type="application/json" id="entry-data">
        {"id":"harvard_vi4_494","series":"Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)","seq":494,"text":"[[2162.1]] <b>388₆.  De controversiis DE CONTROVERSIIS </p>\n<p> [[2162.4]] Controversiae quemadmodum civiles, ita et sacrae vel ad judicium vel ad causam\n[[2162.5]] pertinent, sive ut vulgo loquuntur vel ad Processum judiciarium, vel ad Merita causae. </p>\n<p> [[2162.6]] Controversiae quae ad Judicium ipsum pertinent, nonnunquam generales, praejudiciales,\n[[2162.7]] liminares dicuntur. Est autem <b>judicium status hominum rationibus\n[[2162.8]] certantium sub exitus sive conclusionis spe.</i> Spes autem victoriae a certo\n[[2162.9]] quodam signo visibili ac nullis disputationibus subjecto pendere debet. Quale est sententia\n[[2162.10]] judicis, persuasio ipsius adversarii, evidentia rationis. </p>\n<p> [[2162.11]] Caetera enim signa pleraque novarum saepe difficultatum feracia sunt. Judex si quid\n[[2162.12]] in sententia sua sit ambiguitatis aut obscuritatis, tollere poterit explicando. Fateor tamen\n[[2162.13]] nullo judice opus fore, si duo litigantes in certam quandam disputandi formam consentirent,\n[[2162.14]] eamque accurate observarent, ita enim sponte naturae veritas vel certe probabilitas\n[[2162.15]] alterutrius opinionis se detegeret, <b>et pro judice esset ratio ipsa.</b> </p>\n<p> [[2162.16]] Opponitur judicium <b>Bello</b>, quod est <i>status</i> hominum <i>per vim certantium</i>, ubi nihil\n[[2162.17]] attinet adjicere exitus spem, cum in ipsa hujus certaminis natura contineatur, provalente\n[[2162.18]] utique potentiore aut feliciore: at vero non omnis status per rationes certantium judicium\n[[2162.19]] est, saepe enim abest spes exitus utroque sententiam ad extremum tuente, auditoribusque\n[[2162.20]] suspensis. </p>\n<p> [[2162.21]] Qui rationibus certant vicisse videbuntur, ubi scopum assecuti erunt, scopus autem\n[[2162.22]] est persuadere. Nam qui sorte, qui monomachia, qui purgatione quam vocant, sive\n[[2162.23]] probatione per ignem aut aquam, denique qui tormentis vincit, is non ideo innocentiam\n[[2163.1]] suam aut adversarii culpam persuadet, aufert tamen praemium, impunitatem scilicet aut\n[[2163.2]] rem de qua agitur. </p>\n","number":"388₆.","title":"De controversiis","date":null}
      </script>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers using proper regex
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[([0-9]+\.[0-9]+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Get entry data from JSON script
    const entryDataScript = document.getElementById('entry-data');
    let entryData = null;
    if (entryDataScript) {
      try {
        entryData = JSON.parse(entryDataScript.textContent);
      } catch (e) {
        console.error('Failed to parse entry data:', e);
      }
    }

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entryData && entryData.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entryData.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>